# inflight-row-hook drives the hook under test and the waiter under test (each `!`), and copies the hook's and the
# waiter's siblings into a consumer-layout world: the hook runs snapshot-update.sh, which runs the stamp validator,
# which resolves a LATE candidate through wait-for-deliverable.sh and reads its id grammar from
# validate-adversarial-convergence.sh; the waiter sources wfd-start-of.sh and resolves merge-adversarial-shards.sh.
!core/hooks/ai-dlc-inflight-row.sh
!core/scripts/wait-for-deliverable.sh
core/scripts/snapshot-update.sh
core/scripts/validate-artifact-budget.sh
core/scripts/validate-adversarial-convergence.sh
core/scripts/merge-adversarial-shards.sh
core/scripts/wfd-start-of.sh
# The era gate reads this step file; the fixture installs it, and a copy with the era sentence removed.
!core/skills/ai-dlc/steps/_gate-procedures.md
# The same-run kill helper, sourced by run.sh.
!core/fixtures/lib/mutant.sh
